          "guid": "msqw6fvqtcddcaz0",
          "message": {
            "text": "Protected Apple PostScript names must bypass both by-name entry points. CoreText cannot reopen a dot-prefixed system face by name: it substitutes Times New Roman, after which the existing exact-name guard rejects the result. Skipping the calls preserves the same honest-failure routing while eliminating misleading diagnostics; ordinary names retain the duplicate-installation recovery path.",
            "markdown": "Protected Apple PostScript names must bypass both by-name entry points. CoreText cannot reopen a dot-prefixed system face by name: it substitutes Times New Roman, after which the existing exact-name guard rejects the result. Skipping the calls preserves the same honest-failure routing while eliminating misleading diagnostics; ordinary names retain the duplicate-installation recovery path."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "tools/macos-glyph-extractor/Sources/DomotionGlyphPaths/main.swift"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 300,
                  "endLine": 309,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "    // Apple's protected dot-prefixed system faces cannot be reopened by name:\n    // CoreText substitutes Times New Roman, logs a diagnostic, and the exact-\n    // name guard below necessarily rejects it. Skip only that impossible retry.\n    // A name-only request still reaches the explicit unverified branch below;\n    // ordinary file-backed names retain this recovery path (notably when a\n    // richer duplicate installation carries the requested cut).\n    if !pickedNameMatch, let name = postscriptName, !name.hasPrefix(\".\") {\n        let byName = CTFontCreateWithNameAndOptions(name as CFString, CGFloat(size), nil, .preventAutoActivation)\n        // Verify the by-name lookup found a face whose postscript name actually\n        // matches what we asked for — CTFontCreateWithName falls back to the"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
